Cell["Angular equation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c045e2d2-bbab-4bb9-b761-a1873d6bf67c"],

Cell["\<\
For the angle use the polar form of the hyperbola, s = (1 + e cos v)/(a (e^2 \
\[Minus] 1)). Along the orbit (s+ \[Minus] s)(s \[Minus] s\[Minus]) = e^2 \
sin^2 v/(a^2 (e^2 \[Minus] 1)^2) and ds = \[Minus]e sin v dv/(a (e^2 \[Minus] \
1)), so d\[Phi] = (d\[Phi]/dt) dt = Q(s) (b0 + b1 s) dv.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b63af71a-b5d7-4335-942f-8056928235ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"polar", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"s", "\[Rule]", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"1", "+", 
       RowBox[{"e", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "v", "]"}]}]}], 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["e", "2"], "-", "1"}], ")"}]}]]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fb85248b-2e22-4867-8ae7-47e371d1124d"],

